# Owner Control Console Architecture Rules

## 1. Single Control Plane Principle
- Never instantiate raw browser media tasks (`new AudioContext()`), local canvas frame loops (`requestAnimationFrame`), or video encoding routines inside dashboard views under `components/owner/`.
- Dashboard rooms are **presentational layouts** driven by props from `OwnerBroadcastSnapshot` and related types in `lib/owner/contracts.ts`.
- Canonical behavior reference: `docs/owner-broadcast-contract.md`.
- Media capture, WebRTC publish, and encoder loops belong on dedicated routes (e.g. `/owner/publish/camera`, reachable from Broadcast Control — not a sidebar item) or external services.

## 2. Security Invariant
- Never render raw RTMP ingest URLs, stream keys, or full HLS playback URL strings in attendee surfaces or public API responses.
- **Exception:** `/owner/control` (Broadcast Control wizard) may show RTMP URL + stream key to authenticated `ADMIN_EMAILS` operators via `GET /api/owner/ingest/credentials` only.
- All other owner rooms track pipelines via status badges, "Configured / Missing" tokens, preflight checks, and manifest health.
- All `/owner/**` pages require server-side `requireOwnerUser()` (`ADMIN_EMAILS`) in `app/owner/layout.tsx` before any layout pixels render.

## 3. UI Composition Requirements
- Scope owner console components strictly to **TypeScript** (`.tsx`).
- Group all dashboard rooms under the unified owner layout shell (`app/owner/layout.tsx`).
- Operator-centric **five-room** sidebar navigation:
  - `/owner/pre-show` — Pre-Show Hub (schedule + preflight todos)
  - `/owner/control` — Broadcast Control (go-live, dual-ingest failover)
  - `/owner/video-switcher` — Camera Switcher (preview/program routing)
  - `/owner/audio-monitoring` — Sound Control (VU telemetry + AI gain guard via `POST /api/owner/audio/config`)
  - `/owner/audio-mixing` — Mastering Desk (FX rack config via `POST /api/owner/audio/presets`)
- Go-live actions must respect **pending todos** (preflight fail/warn blockers) before enabling master transmit controls.

## 4. Three Axes (never collapse)
Always show **event phase**, **publish**, and **playback** separately in control surfaces. Do not merge into a single "LIVE" badge.

## 5. Drop Curtain (instant override)
Instant go-live bypasses schedule registries — see `.cursor/rules/owner-drop-curtain-override.mdc` for the non-blocking `current_state = 'imminent_live'` invariant and server-anchored attendee countdown (`dropStartedAt`).

## 6. Responsive layout
Mobile/tablet/desktop scaling uses Tailwind breakpoints only — see `.cursor/rules/owner-responsive.mdc`. No resize listeners in owner rooms.

## 7. Event binding
Critical operator buttons use direct native `onClick` handlers — see `.cursor/rules/owner-event-binding.mdc`.

